# milestone 28 / story 00 — the SEA build recipe's local output (esbuild bundle,
# sidecar assets, sea-config.json, blob, and the built binary). A generated
# artifact, never committed; Story 01's CI matrix produces the signed release
# artifacts separately.
dist-sea/

# Runtime: live agent-terminal session registry (operational, not committed)
.aof/terminal-sessions.json

# NOTE: the mesh record stream (.aof/mesh/) is ignored in .aof/.gitignore, alongside
# the other .aof/ runtime/derived state — not here.

# milestone 36 / story 00 — the Rust Cargo build output for the Mesh Desktop App
# (app/desktop/). Cargo.lock IS committed (an application workspace, not a published
# library) — only the compiled target/ artifact directory is generated/ignored.
app/desktop/target/

# milestone 36 / stories 01-02 — the Tauri shell (crates/app/) is EXCLUDED from the
# app/desktop/ Cargo workspace (its own independent build), so it gets its own
# target/ output dir; and crates/app/gen/ is Tauri's own build-script-generated
# schema/capability output (regenerated every build, never hand-edited).
app/desktop/crates/app/target/
app/desktop/crates/app/gen/

MicrosoftEdgeWebview2Setup.exe 

# aof mesh runtime: per-run git worktrees the worker daemon checks out to execute
# assigned items — a full embedded checkout of this repo, never a record to commit.
# (m43's bundle .gitignore stopped blanket-ignoring .aof/mesh/ because on a real node
# the mesh dir IS the tracked bus; the worktrees under it are still runtime state.)
.aof/mesh/worktrees/
